# PinballWizard reranker-sensitive HARD-eval candidates (v1, pre-classification, 2026-06-30).
# Companion to wizard.v2.jsonl; same row schema (raw OPDB ids, no mch_ prefix) plus the
# hard-set fields slice/source/first_stage_rank (slice + first_stage_rank are written by the
# --probe-retrieval pass, NOT hand-set here). See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-30-rerank-hard-eval-design.md.
#
# Curated against the LIVE pinwiz-rag-v1 index (27,572 chunks / 306 machine_ids), 2026-06-30.
# Every gold citation is a content-bearing id (Manual/Rulesheet/GameOverview), verified by sampling
# the machine's chunks. acceptable_citation_sets cover each machine's edition/alias family so a
# sibling-id resolution does not false-miss (the AFM-Remake drift class, project_eval_noise_and_afm_remake_drift).
# Questions are deliberately over-generated toward reranker-sensitivity (adversarial/title-omitted
# phrasing, theme-confusable cross-machine bait); the probe is the empirical filter — whatever lands
# easy or retrieval-miss is reported honestly, not forced into the headline slice.
#
# source vocabulary: confusable-edition | adversarial-phrasing | corpus-mined
#
